==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|dum}} {{term|loteren||to wobble}} (compare Dutch {{term|leuteren}}). Cognate with Swiss German {{term|lottern||to wobble}}, German {{term|Lotterbube||rascal}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈlɔɪtə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|ˈlɔjɾɚ}}
* {{audio|en-us-loiter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɔɪtə(r)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To stand about without any aim or purpose; to stand about [[idly]]; to [[linger]]; to [[hang around]].
#: ''For some reason, they discourage '''loitering''' outside the store, but encourage it inside.''

